[Help]
Title=How to Use BdoPin
Close=Close
OpenFailed=Could not open help.
What=What does BdoPin do?\n\nBdoPin is a 64-bit Windows application built with .NET Framework 4.8.\n\nBdoPin sets the CPU cores and Windows process priority available to BlackDesert64.exe.\n\nIt does not disable SMT or Hyper-Threading across your system. The selected preset restricts only the logical CPUs available to the Black Desert process. Other programs' CPU settings are not changed.\n\nIf you change TargetProcess in the INI file, BdoPin applies these settings to that process instead.
Why=Why use it?\n\nOn some CPU and game configurations, using selected physical cores or P-cores instead of every logical thread may reduce CPU scheduling interference and improve frame times or occasional stuttering.\n\nThe AMD Ryzen Physical Cores Only preset selects one logical thread per physical core, leaving out the other SMT sibling.\n\nThe Intel P-Cores / Physical Threads preset excludes E-cores and selects one logical thread per P-core, leaving out its other SMT sibling.\n\nBdoPin does not guarantee higher FPS. Results depend on your CPU, Windows version, game version and system configuration. Compare performance before and after applying a preset.
QuickStart=Quick start\n\n1. Check that your CPU vendor was detected correctly.\n\n2. Select the preset you want to use.\n\n3. Review the Selected Logical CPUs list.\n\n4. Choose Process Priority. The default is Above Normal.\n\n5. Start Black Desert.\n\n6. If automatic application is enabled and process detection is available, BdoPin applies your settings when the game starts.\n\n7. If automatic detection is unavailable, start the game and click Apply Now.\n\n8. Click Remove Settings to enable all available logical CPUs and restore Normal priority. Your saved preset, priority selection and Auto Apply option are unchanged; the next game launch can apply them again.\n\nCheck Last Apply for the time, PID and success or failure result.
Permissions=About permissions\n\nApply Now and Remove Settings first try with the current privileges. Only an access-denied result requests a Windows UAC restart, after which the selected action is performed automatically.\n\nCancelling keeps the existing window. Access may still be denied as administrator; BdoPin does not repeatedly request elevation.\n\nAuto Apply never requests UAC. WMI detection permissions are separate from game process access. Use Apply Now if automatic detection is unavailable.
Safety=Safety\n\nBdoPin does not:\n\n- Read or write game memory\n- Inject DLLs\n- Install hooks\n- Patch code\n- Install kernel drivers\n- Modify game files\n- Bypass anti-cheat\n\nBdoPin uses documented Windows APIs to set process affinity and process priority only.

